  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 253 PM CDT Fri Sep 11 2026\n\nDeterministic guidance pushes the cold front south of I-70/I-64 by \nlate Sunday night/early Monday, but an upper level short wave ridge \nbuilds into the Midwest by 12Z Monday morning which brings the front \nto a final stop.  The models print out precip along the front Sunday \ninto Sunday night as the low level jet continues to ride over the \ncooler air at the surface.  The precip reinforces the boundary in \nthe deterministic guidance, but the next upstream short wave \nincreases southwest flow over the Great Plains and pushes the front \nback into Iowa and northern Illinois by late Monday night.  While \ntemperatures will be cooler in the low to mid 80s north of the front \nacross northeast Missouri into west central Illinois Sunday and \nMonday, most areas farther south will likely continue in the upper \n80s to around 90.  Ensemble guidance does show quite a bit of \nvariance in temperatures with max temp IQRs in excess of 5 degrees on \nSunday and as much as 10-12 degrees on Monday.  While temperatures \ndo steady out Tuesday and Wednesday in the upper 80s to low 90s \nacross the area with the front in Iowa, much uncertainty remains for \nthe latter half of the week as the upper ridge breaks down and the \nfront drifts back into Missouri and central/southern Illinois. The \nLREF temperature IQRs increase to 15+ degrees for Thursday and \nFriday and precipitation chances increase again as the front moves \ninto and through the forecast area.",
